% ====================================================
% REPEAT — Isaiah 63:1–6
% Source: blue ink, photo 45 (PXL_20261105_235847391.jpg)
% Compare with: Isaiah/63.tex (black ink, photo 48)
% ====================================================
  \pb \verse{63:1} Who is this coming from Edom?\pa With dyed\alt{garments} clothes from Bozrah?%%

  \pb Who is glorious in appearance,\pa traveling in the greatness\alt{majesty, abundance} of His power?\alt{strength?}%%

  \pb ``I, speaking in righteousness,\pa am mighty to save.''%%

  \pb \verse{63:2} ``Why are your clothes red?\pa And thy garments look like they've been trodden in a wine press?''%%

  \pb \verse{63:3} ``I have trodden the winepress alone~---\pa not a man from among the people was with Me.%%

  \pb I tread them in Mine anger,\pa yea, I tread\alt{trample} them in My fury.%%

  \pb Their strength\alt{blood} is sprinkled on My garments\pa and all My clothes are stained.%%

  \pb \verse{63:4} For the day of vengeance\alt{Mine avenged} is in My heart~---\pa the year of My Redeemer is here!\alt{has come!}%%

  \pb \verse{63:5} I looked and there was no helper;\alt{none to help;}\pa I am astonished that there is none to support,%%

  \pb and \understood{give} salvation to Mine arm~---\pa My wrath hath supported Me.%%

  \pb \verse{63:6} I tread down people in Mine anger;\pa I make them drunk in\alt{by} My fury.\alt{rage.}%%

  \pb And I bring their blood\alt{strength} down to the earth.''%%
